## Genre layouts — where each archetype slots

### Repository teardown (`*-repo-teardown.mdx`)

| Essay moment | Figure (binding) | Why this archetype |
| --- | --- | --- |
| The components/architecture table | `LayerStack` (accordion-layer-stack) | disclosure is the right shape for a stack; order carries structure |
| Key findings / evidence mix | `MetricMatrix` (column-sort-matrix) | lets the reader sort claims by evidence kind — including "not measured" |
| The adoption/deployment checklist | `AssumptionSwitches` (toggle-assumption-inference) | a checklist is a set of earned assumptions |
| Before "What remains unverified?" | `SelfCheckQuiz` (answer-reveal-quiz) | the reader audits the review before citing it |
| (optional) A cost/complexity split | `BudgetSplit` (partition-drag-allocation) | where the fixed budget concentrates |

### Methods essay (statistics, benchmarking, reviewing)

| Essay moment | Figure (binding) | Why |
| --- | --- | --- |
| The taxonomy table (misreadings, fallacies) | `MetricMatrix` | sort by error type |
| The model behind the claims | `AssumptionSwitches` | flip assumptions, watch what the claim supports |
| "Read the paragraph/figure like this" | `HotspotAtlas` (pinned-hotspot-annotation) | anchored pins, reading-order tour |
| Recall check near the end | `SelfCheckQuiz` | commit before quoting |
| A worked number evolving | `RacePlayback` (playback-race-series) | only with *computed* values, never invented ones |

### Site/meta post (`welcome-*`, `notes-*`)

| Essay moment | Figure (binding) | Why |
| --- | --- | --- |
| "What a page here is made of" | `HotspotAtlas` | anatomy pins in reading order |
| The enforced gates | `MetricMatrix` | real budgets, sortable |
| A real budget split | `BudgetSplit` | caps are real, shares labelled illustrative |
| How the machine works | `SelfCheckQuiz` | every answer is on the page |

### DO NOT force-fit

No `WipeCompare` without two full fields of the same shape; no `TradeoffPad`
without a genuine 2-D parameter space with honest (linear) outcomes; no
`LensPeek` without a real derived layer. If the essay has no data of that
shape, the essay does not get that archetype — pick from the 13 available.

---

## The problem in one paragraph

Answer-first prose. The first paragraph of the body is 40–60 words and
states the finding, not the itinerary (check:site enforces this).

## Section one — the concept

Lead-in sentence naming the question, then the figure:

<__FIGURE_1__ />

Read the default state aloud: what the reader sees before touching anything,
and what changes when they do.

## Section two — the mechanism

A different archetype for a different kind of understanding:

<__FIGURE_2__ />

## The evidence

Tables and result charts carry evidence; interactive figures carry
mechanisms. Keep the two apart.

